libjbytecode
Copyright (c) 2026 luiox

This product is an independent C++17 implementation of the JVM classfile
reading/writing/transform pipeline. It is API-compatible with, and behaviourally
validated against, ObjectWeb ASM (https://github.com/JetBrains/asm), but it is
not a derivative work of it: libjbytecode implements its own parser, tree model,
visitor framework and bytecode writers. The round-trip boundary is documented in
doc/safety.md — notably, identical input does NOT guarantee byte-identical
output versus the ASM Java implementation.

Earlier revisions of this library contained two functions derived from
ObjectWeb ASM (`Constants::isWhitelisted()` and `Constants::checkIsPreview()`,
originally marked in-source as "Ported from org.objectweb.asm.Constants").
Those functions were unused by the library and by all of its consumers, and
they have been removed. No ASM-derived code remains in this source tree.

Third-party dependencies are declared in xmake.lua and are not vendored here.

Portions of the test suite reference vectors and expectations published in the
JVM Specification (JVMS) and FIPS 46-3; these are factual standards documents,
not copyrighted source code.